# tools/ales_stereo_reverb_shelf_witness.rish — the stereo shelf: a two-band tone shelf on the reverberant tail carried across a stereo master (ALES205).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES205.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-112822_fill-ales205-lotus-stereo-reverb-shelf.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye (ALES191 — the named-room stereo wet, run over the master unchanged); lotus/shelf.rye (ALES41 — the
# two-band tone shelf, its precheck and its BadCoeff / BadGain / BadRange, run per ear); lotus/reverb_shelf.rye (ALES204 — the mono shelf this mirrors
# per channel); lotus/pan.rye (the StereoClip and its two balanced channels); lotus/clock.rye (ALES5 — the sample clock, converting the span);
# lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip each channel holds, its max_clip bounding the span and its saturate the shelf's single rail).
#
# lotus/stereo_reverb_shelf.rye carries ALES204's two-band reverb EQ across a stereo master — the SAME shelf over BOTH channels of a StereoClip, one
# shared bass, treble, and split, the image held. ALES199 carried only the plain darkness knob across; the full two-band shelf stopped at mono until
# this rung. It reverberates the master WET in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset UNCHANGED, prechecks the shelf setting (the SAME guards
# ALES41 raises) BEFORE the wet is written so a bad setting leaves both channels DRY and balanced (the atomicity crux), then tone-shelves EACH channel's
# wet at the SAME setting with NO cross-channel read — the left ear shelves left, the right ear shelves right, so the image the preset held is held. No
# new audio arithmetic — every shelved sample is written by a proven stage, each band scaled in the wide i64 domain and saturated ONCE. The selftest
# proves on both channels: at bass == unity AND treble == unity the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a real shelf each channel equals
# stereo_reverb_preset then shelf.shelf on that channel byte for byte and each shelved channel differs from its wet; each treble-cut channel's
# high-frequency roughness is strictly less than its wet's (the treble cut darkens) and each bass-boost channel's total energy is strictly greater than
# its wet's (the bass boost lifts); the image is held (a centred master identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master distinct — no crossing); the
# channels leave balanced and silence stays silence; and the faults forward atomic (an illegal coefficient BadCoeff, a zero band denominator BadGain
# with both channels still dry, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange). Purely local — one StereoClip, a validated clock;
# no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_reverb_shelf_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: Language EN — ALES204 gave the MONO reverb its two-band shelving EQ (bass and treble each boosting OR cutting its own band of the tail independently, so the wash sits warm and dark, bright and airy, or thinned of mud). Yet a keeper mixing a STEREO master had only the plain darkness knob carried across (ALES199); the full shelf stopped at mono. This rung is the thin twin ALES204 named next — the SAME shelf over both channels, one shared bass, treble, and split — and it invents no new primitive, since ALES41's two-band shelf already stands, so the stereo reverb EQ is a clean composition of proven stages run per ear."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: Style Radiant — the identity edge is stated positively and proven exact on BOTH channels: at bass == unity AND treble == unity the span equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte (a flat EQ is the un-shelved stereo reverb); a bass boost lifts the low wash so each shelved channel's total energy strictly exceeds its wet's, and a treble cut darkens each so its high-frequency roughness falls strictly below its wet's. The image is held — a centred master stays identical channel-to-channel, a genuinely stereo master keeps its channels distinct, no crossing — because the left ear shelves left and the right ear shelves right with one shared setting."
say "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: Lens TAME — one StereoClip of i16 PCM, a validated clock, and ALES191's fixed banks; NO new audio arithmetic — the shelf is ALES41's proven two-band shelf over the proven stereo wet, run per ear, each band scaled in the wide i64 domain and saturated ONCE; StereoReverbShelfError = stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || shelf.ShelfError, the shelf setting PRECHECKED before the wet is written (the same guards ALES41 raises) so a bad shelf leaves both channels dry and balanced (atomic), DurationTooLong / BadRange / BadCoeff / BadGain by name before any write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device. A wet-tail stereo shelf; the split is a fraction per sample index (a crossover in hertz a later rung)."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_shelf"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_shelf.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_shelf.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-shelf' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-shelf line"

# This rung runs ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset over its public API for the wet — re-prove the named-room stereo preset still stands green beside it.
let preset = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_reverb_preset.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset && lotus/bin/stereo_reverb_preset selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-preset' && echo yes"]
assert (trim preset.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: the ALES191 named-room stereo preset regressed under its shelf"

# And re-prove ALES41's two-band tone shelf still stands green — the shelving it applies to each ear.
let shelf = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/shelf.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/shelf && lotus/bin/shelf selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-shelf' && echo yes"]
assert (trim shelf.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: the ALES41 two-band shelf regressed under its stereo reverb shelf"

# And re-prove ALES204's mono reverb shelf still stands green — the mono rung this mirrors per ear.
let mono = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/reverb_shelf.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/reverb_shelf && lotus/bin/reverb_shelf selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb-shelf' && echo yes"]
assert (trim mono.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: the ALES204 mono reverb shelf regressed beside its stereo twin"

say "ales-stereo-reverb-shelf: GREEN — the stereo shelf: a two-band tone shelf on the reverberant tail carried across a stereo master. Reverberate the master wet in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, then tone-shelf each channel's wet with ALES41's proven two-band shelf at the same setting, no cross-channel read — bass == unity AND treble == unity the identity, a bass boost lifting the low wash, a treble cut darkening the tail — no new audio arithmetic. Proven on both channels: at bass == unity AND treble == unity exactly stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte; for a real shelf each channel equals stereo_reverb_preset then shelf.shelf on that channel byte for byte and differs from its wet; each treble-cut channel's roughness is strictly less than its wet's (darkens) and each bass-boost channel's energy is strictly greater than its wet's (lifts); the image is held (centred identical, stereo distinct); the channels leave balanced and silence stays silence; an illegal coefficient refuses BadCoeff, a zero band denominator BadGain with both channels still dry, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving both channels untouched; the ALES191 stereo preset, the ALES41 shelf, and the ALES204 mono shelf stay GREEN beside it. The tone axis now stands whole for mono and stereo in both its plain-darkness and full-shelf forms; a fresh reverb axis (width, freeze, or early/late balance) is next."
